  "body": "I have a problem about mail registration such as an user can submit a new element's account by our custom server .\r\nI trace the log and it shows an error message in the blow.\r\n\r\n2022-03-25 09:38:38,238 - synapse.http.client - 455 - INFO - POST-18 - Error sending request to  POST https://mail.element.abc/_matrix/identity/api/v1/validate/email/requestToken: RequestTransmissionFailed [<twisted.python.failure.Failure service_identity.exceptions.VerificationError: VerificationError(errors=[DNSMismatch(mismatched_id=DNS_ID(hostname=b'mail.element.abc'))])>]\r\n\r\nWhatever, I am not sure which problem cause by DNS , homeserver ,or mail setting.\r\nBut I just finish the matrix-synapse, nginx, and postfix installation.\r\n\r\nThe custom server is running well now and I hope to supply the mail registration. \r\nTherefore, all users can use this funtion to reset password when they forget their original pw. ",
